config BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC_AF
	bool "majestic-af"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_MAJESTIC
	help
	  Out-of-core motor driver and autofocus engine for majestic, compiled
	  from source. majestic loads /usr/lib/majestic-af.so at runtime when a
	  motorized lens is declared and the majestic binary exports the plugin
	  HAL seams; the contrast search, the motorized-lens UART actuator
	  (XiongMai near-Pelco and standard Pelco-D), and the worker threads
	  live here.

	  It is the ONLY writer on that UART, and it is now required for manual
	  PTZ as well as autofocus: the WebUI asks majestic for a verb over its
	  HTTP API rather than shipping its own Pelco scripts, which used to
	  open the same tty behind the daemon's back. A camera with
	  ptz_control=pelco-d or pelco-xm and no driver keeps its pad but says
	  what is missing, rather than claiming the camera has no PTZ.

	  https://github.com/OpenIPC/majestic-af
